## Broken (game-verified 2026-08-29, OP 1.29.5 / OpenplanetNext, master @ 7204c86)

Misuses passed **directly** into a typedb funcdef-typed parameter slot are silently accepted by `openplanet-lsp check` while the game compiler rejects them. The ctor form is correct (GH #63 / B022); this is the overload-set call path.

Repro:

```angelscript
void Good(UI::InputTextCallbackData@ data) { data.SelectAll(); }
void WrongSig(int x) {}
void Render() {
    string s = "test";
    // A: game ERR, LSP silent
    UI::InputText("##a", s, UI::InputTextFlags::None, WrongSig);
    // B: game ERR, LSP silent
    UI::InputText("##b", s, UI::InputTextFlags::None, "nope");
    // C: correctly flagged by both
    UI::InputTextCallback@ c = UI::InputTextCallback(WrongSig);
}
```

Game ground truth (RemoteBuild probe, `scripts/issue_repro_game.py`):

```
(6,5)  ERR: No matching signatures to 'UI::InputText(const string, string, const UI::InputTextFlags, ::WrongSig)'
(8,5)  ERR: No matching signatures to 'UI::InputText(const string, string, const UI::InputTextFlags, const string)'
(10,32) ERR: Can't implicitly convert from '<function>@const' to 'UI::InputTextCallback@&'.
```

LSP: 0 errors (C only: `argument 1 of 'UI::InputTextCallback': expected 'void (UI::InputTextCallbackData@)', got 'void (int)'`).

## Root cause

`check_external_overload_set` (`src/typecheck/checker.rs`, GH #47 machinery) never rejects a candidate on function-shaped args — its FP guard is "Named/unknown-shape args never reject a candidate on their own". A bare function identifier resolves via `lookup_global_value_type` to `TypeRepr::Funcdef("WrongSig")`, which is not name-equivalent to the param, so `funcdef_handle_compatible` is false — but the arg then just fails to produce *evidence*, both 4-arg candidates stay "compatible", and nothing is emitted. The ctor path already has the needed signature-match helpers (`arg_binds_to_funcdef`, `lookup_arg_function_sigs`, `func_matches_funcdef`); the overload-set path doesn't use them for candidate rejection.

## Expected

Mirror the game: when a candidate's funcdef-typed param cannot bind the arg (arg is a resolvable function with an incompatible signature, or provably not a function such as a string literal), that candidate is rejected; if no candidate binds, emit `NoMatchingSignatures` (like GH #47 does for bool-literal-into-`&out`).

## Not

- Do not reject Named/unknown-shape args (workspace classes the typedb can't see, `auto`) — the existing FP guard for those must stay.
- Do not touch the ctor path; it is already correct.
- Legal patterns must stay silent (regression fixture `63-inputtext-callback-funcdef` asserts 0 diagnostics).

## Test plan (TDD, red first; generalize per CLAUDE.md)

- Wrong-signature function into `UI::InputText` / `UI::InputTextMultiline` callback slot → error.
- String literal (non-function) into the slot → error.
- Generalize to other funcdef families: wrong-sig fn into `startnew(...)` (CoroutineFunc family) and a UI::NodTree callback slot if reachable.
- Variants of the matching-fn case: `void(UI::InputTextCallbackData@)` free fn, class method, funcdef-typed local, ctor-wrapped fn — all stay silent.
- Correctly-typed but wrong-signature funcdef-typed variable (`void(int)` stored in a funcdef handle) if representable.
- New `tests/fixtures/issue-repros/<n>-*` fixture asserting diagnosis (47-style), game ground truth via `scripts/issue_repro_game.py`.

## Fix sketch

In `check_external_overload_set`, for each candidate param that resolves to a typedb funcdef (`GlobalScope::lookup_funcdef`), run the same bind test as `check_funcdef_ctor_arg`; a resolvable-function arg that matches no candidate's signature — or a literal that is clearly not a function — is rejection evidence. Reuse `is_clearly_not_a_function` for the literal case.

Decision (2026-08-29, coordinator): implemented after B027 in the same lane/worktree — both edit src/typecheck/checker.rs (serial by file overlap); B027's mode plumbing (extract_params + func_matches_funcdef) is a prerequisite so overload-path signature comparison sees real &out modes. Ops: wrap EVERY scripts/issue_repro_game.py run in: flock /tmp/lsp-openplanet-game-probe.lock -c '<cmd>'.

Resolved (2026-08-29). check_external_overload_set and the unique-overload path now run the ctor-path bind test (mode-correct post-B027) on candidate funcdef slots: resolvable functions matching no signature, incompatible funcdef-typed values, and provably non-function values (null stays neutral) reject the candidate; NoMatchingSignatures when none binds. Review-added: a function-shaped value at a KNOWN non-funcdef param also rejects (game positional-binding parity — it closes the shifted-overload hole on the coordinator's 4-arg repro). GH #47 Named/unknown FP guard intact (unit-tested); ctor path untouched. Fixture b023-funcdef-slot-signatures: LSP = game line-for-line (7 reject / 6 legal); coordinator repro fully flagged. KNOWN false-negative (probe 2026-08-29): a LOCAL class-handle shadowing a same-named global fn passed to a funcdef slot — game ERRs, LSP stays neutral by B023's Named-shape FP guard (test function_arg_ident_local_class_handle_shadow_stays_neutral pins the chosen behavior; file a follow-up if parity wanted). Commit a734d5f + b670e42 + 43c4eb0, merged d56af58. Reviews: APPROVE + delta APPROVE.